IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc12-logic`

-- ccc12-part9-false-pretences.l4 -- Criminal Code (Canada), Part IX, "False Pretences": sections 361 to 365.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30); not the official text.
-- Reading a result: see the header of ccc12-part9-theft.l4 and NOTES.md ("Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING (ccc12)").
-- Answers taken from another provision are INPUTS named for that provision (`s 2 <term>: ...`, `s 361(1) ...`, `s 787(1) ...`); never turn NOTHING into FALSE.

§ `False Pretences (ss 361 to 365)`

§§ `Section 361 -- false pretence`

-- src:6995 | False pretence
-- src:6996 | 361 (1) A false pretence is a representation of a matter of fact either present or past, made by words or otherwise, that is known by the person who makes it to be false and that is made with a fraudulent intent to induce the person to whom it is made to act on it.
@ref Criminal Code s 361(1) (src:6995-6996)
GIVEN `it is a representation of a matter of fact either present or past, made by words or otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is known by the person who makes it to be false` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is made with a fraudulent intent to induce the person to whom it is made to act on it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 361(1) the representation is a false pretence` MEANS
    IF    `it is a representation of a matter of fact either present or past, made by words or otherwise`
      AND `it is known by the person who makes it to be false`
      AND `it is made with a fraudulent intent to induce the person to whom it is made to act on it`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A false pretence is a representation of a matter of fact either present or past, made by words or otherwise, that is known by the person who makes it to be false and that is made with a fraudulent intent to induce the person to whom it is made to act on it"

-- src:6997 | Exaggeration
-- src:6998 | (2) Exaggerated commendation or depreciation of the quality of anything is not a false pretence unless it is carried to such an extent that it amounts to a fraudulent misrepresentation of fact.
@ref Criminal Code s 361(2) (src:6997-6998)
GIVEN `the statement is exaggerated commendation or depreciation of the quality of anything` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is carried to such an extent that it amounts to a fraudulent misrepresentation of fact` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 361(2) the exaggerated commendation or depreciation is a false pretence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the statement is exaggerated commendation or depreciation of the quality of anything`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks only of exaggerated commendation or depreciation of the quality of anything
        IF `it is carried to such an extent that it amounts to a fraudulent misrepresentation of fact`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "unless it is carried to such an extent that it amounts to a fraudulent misrepresentation of fact": the "unless" met lifts the exclusion but the subsection does not itself say that it is a false pretence (fork F-UNLESS)
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Exaggerated commendation or depreciation of the quality of anything is not a false pretence"

-- src:6999 | Question of fact
-- src:7000 | (3) For the purposes of subsection (2), it is a question of fact whether commendation or depreciation amounts to a fraudulent misrepresentation of fact.
@ref Criminal Code s 361(3) (src:6999-7000)
GIVEN `the question is whether the commendation or depreciation amounts to a fraudulent misrepresentation of fact` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 361(3) the question is a question of fact` MEANS
    IF `the question is whether the commendation or depreciation amounts to a fraudulent misrepresentation of fact`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection says that this question is a question of fact; it says nothing of any other

§§ `Section 362 -- false pretence or false statement`

DECLARE `s 362(1)(c) thing procured` IS ONE OF
    `s 362(1)(c)(i) the delivery of personal property`
    `s 362(1)(c)(ii) the payment of money`
    `s 362(1)(c)(iii) the making of a loan`
    `s 362(1)(c)(iv) the grant or extension of credit`
    `s 362(1)(c)(v) the discount of an account receivable`
    `s 362(1)(c)(vi) the making, accepting, discounting or endorsing of a bill of exchange, cheque, draft or promissory note`
    `s 362(1)(c) none of those`

-- src:7001 | False pretence or false statement
-- src:7002 | 362 (1) Every one commits an offence who
-- src:7003 | (a) by a false pretence, whether directly or through the medium of a contract obtained by a false pretence, obtains anything in respect of which the offence of theft may be committed or causes it to be delivered to another person;
-- src:7004 | (b) obtains credit by a false pretence or by fraud;
-- src:7005 | (c) knowingly makes or causes to be made, directly or indirectly, a false statement in writing with intent that it should be relied on, with respect to the financial condition or means or ability to pay of himself or herself or any person or organization that he or she is interested in or that he or she acts for, for the purpose of procuring, in any form whatever, whether for his or her benefit or the benefit of that person or organization,
-- src:7006 | (i) the delivery of personal property,
-- src:7007 | (ii) the payment of money,
-- src:7008 | (iii) the making of a loan,
-- src:7009 | (iv) the grant or extension of credit,
-- src:7010 | (v) the discount of an account receivable, or
-- src:7011 | (vi) the making, accepting, discounting or endorsing of a bill of exchange, cheque, draft or promissory note; or
-- src:7012 | (d) knowing that a false statement in writing has been made with respect to the financial condition or means or ability to pay of himself or herself or another person or organization that he or she is interested in or that he or she acts for, procures on the faith of that statement, whether for his or her benefit or for the benefit of that person or organization, anything mentioned in subparagraphs (c)(i) to (vi).
@ref Criminal Code s 362(1) (src:7001-7012)
GIVEN `the person obtains anything in respect of which the offence of theft may be committed, or causes it to be delivered to another person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the means is a false pretence, whether directly or through the medium of a contract obtained by a false pretence, by s 361(1) the representation is a false pretence` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 362(1)(a) the person commits the offence of obtaining a thing by a false pretence` MEANS
    IF `the person obtains anything in respect of which the offence of theft may be committed, or causes it to be delivered to another person`
    THEN `the means is a false pretence, whether directly or through the medium of a contract obtained by a false pretence, by s 361(1) the representation is a false pretence`   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text) where the s 361(1) answer was not given
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every one commits an offence who (a) by a false pretence, whether directly or through the medium of a contract obtained by a false pretence, obtains anything in respect of which the offence of theft may be committed or causes it to be delivered to another person"

@ref Criminal Code s 362(1) (src:7004-7004)
GIVEN `the person obtains credit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person does so by a false pretence, by s 361(1) the representation is a false pretence` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person does so by fraud` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 362(1)(b) the person commits the offence of obtaining credit by a false pretence or by fraud` MEANS
    IF `the person obtains credit`
    THEN `ccc12 or` `the person does so by a false pretence, by s 361(1) the representation is a false pretence` (JUST `the person does so by fraud`)
         -- JUST FALSE where the pretence is a definite no and there was no fraud: FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) obtains credit by a false pretence or by fraud"
         -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): where the s 361(1) answer was not given and there was no fraud
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every one commits an offence who ... (b) obtains credit by a false pretence or by fraud"

@ref Criminal Code s 362(1) (src:7005-7011)
GIVEN `the person knowingly makes or causes to be made, directly or indirectly, a false statement in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person does so with intent that it should be relied on` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement is with respect to the financial condition or means or ability to pay of the person or of any person or organization that the person is interested in or acts for` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing the person does so for the purpose of procuring, in any form whatever, whether for the person's benefit or the benefit of that person or organization` IS A `s 362(1)(c) thing procured`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 362(1)(c) the person commits the offence of making a false statement in writing about financial condition or means to procure a benefit` MEANS
    IF    `the person knowingly makes or causes to be made, directly or indirectly, a false statement in writing`
      AND `the person does so with intent that it should be relied on`
      AND `the statement is with respect to the financial condition or means or ability to pay of the person or of any person or organization that the person is interested in or acts for`
    THEN CONSIDER `the thing the person does so for the purpose of procuring, in any form whatever, whether for the person's benefit or the benefit of that person or organization`
         WHEN `s 362(1)(c)(i) the delivery of personal property` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 362(1)(c)(ii) the payment of money` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 362(1)(c)(iii) the making of a loan` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 362(1)(c)(iv) the grant or extension of credit` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 362(1)(c)(v) the discount of an account receivable` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 362(1)(c)(vi) the making, accepting, discounting or endorsing of a bill of exchange, cheque, draft or promissory note` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 362(1)(c) none of those` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "for the purpose of procuring, in any form whatever, whether for his or her benefit or the benefit of that person or organization, (i) the delivery of personal property, (ii) the payment of money, (iii) the making of a loan, (iv) the grant or extension of credit, (v) the discount of an account receivable, or (vi) the making, accepting, discounting or endorsing of a bill of exchange, cheque, draft or promissory note"
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(c) knowingly makes or causes to be made, directly or indirectly, a false statement in writing with intent that it should be relied on, with respect to the financial condition or means or ability to pay of himself or herself or any person or organization that he or she is interested in or that he or she acts for"

@ref Criminal Code s 362(1) (src:7012-7012)
GIVEN `the person knows that a false statement in writing has been made with respect to the financial condition or means or ability to pay of the person or of another person or organization that the person is interested in or acts for` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing the person procures on the faith of that statement, whether for the person's benefit or for the benefit of that person or organization` IS A `s 362(1)(c) thing procured`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 362(1)(d) the person commits the offence of procuring a benefit on the faith of a false statement in writing` MEANS
    IF `the person knows that a false statement in writing has been made with respect to the financial condition or means or ability to pay of the person or of another person or organization that the person is interested in or acts for`
    THEN CONSIDER `the thing the person procures on the faith of that statement, whether for the person's benefit or for the benefit of that person or organization`
         WHEN `s 362(1)(c)(i) the delivery of personal property` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 362(1)(c)(ii) the payment of money` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 362(1)(c)(iii) the making of a loan` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 362(1)(c)(iv) the grant or extension of credit` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 362(1)(c)(v) the discount of an account receivable` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 362(1)(c)(vi) the making, accepting, discounting or endorsing of a bill of exchange, cheque, draft or promissory note` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 362(1)(c) none of those` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "anything mentioned in subparagraphs (c)(i) to (vi)"
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(d) knowing that a false statement in writing has been made with respect to the financial condition or means or ability to pay of himself or herself or another person or organization that he or she is interested in or that he or she acts for, procures on the faith of that statement"

-- The offence of subsection (1) as a whole: one of paragraphs (a) to (d) (each answered by its own function above).
-- src:7001 | False pretence or false statement
@ref Criminal Code s 362(1) offence (src:7001)
GIVEN `the person commits the offence under paragraph (a), by s 362(1)(a)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person commits the offence under paragraph (b), by s 362(1)(b)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person commits the offence under paragraph (c), by s 362(1)(c)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person commits the offence under paragraph (d), by s 362(1)(d)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 362(1) the person commits the offence of false pretence or false statement` MEANS
    `ccc12 or` (`ccc12 or` `the person commits the offence under paragraph (a), by s 362(1)(a)` `the person commits the offence under paragraph (b), by s 362(1)(b)`)
               (`ccc12 or` `the person commits the offence under paragraph (c), by s 362(1)(c)` `the person commits the offence under paragraph (d), by s 362(1)(d)`)
    -- JUST FALSE only where all four paragraphs are definite no's: FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every one commits an offence who"
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): where a paragraph's answer was not given and none holds

-- src:7013 | Punishment
-- src:7014 | (2) Every one who commits an offence under paragraph (1)(a)
-- src:7015 | (a) if the property obtained is a testamentary instrument or the value of what is obtained is more than $5,000, is guilty of
-- src:7016 | (i) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 10 years, or
-- src:7017 | (ii) an offence punishable on summary conviction; or
-- src:7018 | (b) if the value of what is obtained is not more than $5,000, is guilty
-- src:7019 | (i) of an indictable offence and is liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding two years, or
-- src:7020 | (ii) of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref Criminal Code s 362(2) (src:7013-7020)
GIVEN `the property obtained is a testamentary instrument, by s 2 testamentary instrument` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the value of what is obtained, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF Punishment)
`s 362(2) the punishment for an offence under paragraph (1)(a)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `ccc12 or` `the property obtained is a testamentary instrument, by s 2 testamentary instrument` (JUST (`the value of what is obtained, in dollars` GREATER THAN 5000))
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST (LIST `ccc12 an indictable limb` (`imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`)   -- (a)(i) indictable offence, imprisonment for a term of not more than 10 years
                                  , `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`)   -- (a)(ii)
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST (LIST `ccc12 an indictable limb` (`imprisonment for a term of` `two years`)   -- (b)(i) indictable offence, imprisonment for a term not exceeding two years
                                   , `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`)   -- (b)(ii)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the s 2 "testamentary instrument" answer was not given and the value is not more than $5,000

-- src:7021 | Idem
-- src:7022 | (3) Every person who commits an offence under paragraph (1)(b), (c) or (d) is guilty of
-- src:7023 | (a) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 10 years; or
-- src:7024 | (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref Criminal Code s 362(3) (src:7021-7024)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 362(3) the punishment for an offence under paragraph (1)(b), (c) or (d)` MEANS
    LIST `ccc12 an indictable limb` (`imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`)   -- (a) indictable offence, imprisonment for a term of not more than 10 years
       , `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`   -- (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction

-- (4): "it shall be presumed ... unless the court is satisfied by evidence that when the accused issued the cheque he believed on reasonable grounds that it would be honoured": the "unless" once met takes the presumption away (JUST FALSE).
-- src:7025 | Presumption from cheque issued without funds
-- src:7026 | (4) Where, in proceedings under paragraph (1)(a), it is shown that anything was obtained by the accused by means of a cheque that, when presented for payment within a reasonable time, was dishonoured on the ground that no funds or insufficient funds were on deposit to the credit of the accused in the bank or other institution on which the cheque was drawn, it shall be presumed to have been obtained by a false pretence, unless the court is satisfied by evidence that when the accused issued the cheque he believed on reasonable grounds that it would be honoured if presented for payment within a reasonable time after it was issued.
@ref Criminal Code s 362(4) (src:7025-7026)
GIVEN `the proceedings are proceedings under paragraph 362(1)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is shown that anything was obtained by the accused by means of a cheque` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the cheque, when presented for payment within a reasonable time, was dishonoured on the ground that no funds or insufficient funds were on deposit to the credit of the accused in the bank or other institution on which the cheque was drawn` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied by evidence that when the accused issued the cheque the accused believed on reasonable grounds that it would be honoured if presented for payment within a reasonable time after it was issued` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 362(4) the thing is presumed to have been obtained by a false pretence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the proceedings are proceedings under paragraph 362(1)(a)` AND `it is shown that anything was obtained by the accused by means of a cheque` AND `the cheque, when presented for payment within a reasonable time, was dishonoured on the ground that no funds or insufficient funds were on deposit to the credit of the accused in the bank or other institution on which the cheque was drawn`)
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where, in proceedings under paragraph (1)(a), it is shown that anything was obtained by the accused by means of a cheque that, when presented for payment within a reasonable time, was dishonoured on the ground that no funds or insufficient funds were on deposit" (a "Where" gate unmet: ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))
        IF `the court is satisfied by evidence that when the accused issued the cheque the accused believed on reasonable grounds that it would be honoured if presented for payment within a reasonable time after it was issued`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it shall be presumed to have been obtained by a false pretence, unless the court is satisfied by evidence that when the accused issued the cheque he believed on reasonable grounds that it would be honoured if presented for payment within a reasonable time after it was issued"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `s 362(5) kind of instrument` IS ONE OF
    `s 362(5) a cheque in its ordinary meaning`
    `s 362(5) a bill of exchange drawn on an institution that makes it a business practice to honour bills of exchange or any particular kind thereof drawn on it by depositors`
    `s 362(5) another instrument`

-- src:7027 | Definition of cheque
-- src:7028 | (5) In this section, cheque includes, in addition to its ordinary meaning, a bill of exchange drawn on any institution that makes it a business practice to honour bills of exchange or any particular kind thereof drawn on it by depositors.
@ref Criminal Code s 362(5) (src:7027-7028)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 362(5) kind of instrument`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 362(5) the instrument is a cheque` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 362(5) a cheque in its ordinary meaning` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 362(5) a bill of exchange drawn on an institution that makes it a business practice to honour bills of exchange or any particular kind thereof drawn on it by depositors` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 362(5) another instrument` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "cheque includes, in addition to its ordinary meaning, a bill of exchange drawn on any institution ..." does not close the list

§§ `Sections 363 to 365 -- valuable security, food, beverage or accommodation`

-- src:7029 | Obtaining execution of valuable security by fraud
-- src:7030 | 363 Every person is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than five years or is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction who, with intent to defraud or injure another person, by a false pretence causes or induces any person
-- src:7031 | (a) to execute, make, accept, endorse or destroy the whole or any part of a valuable security, or
-- src:7032 | (b) to write, impress or affix a name or seal on any paper or parchment in order that it may afterwards be made or converted into or used or dealt with as a valuable security.
@ref Criminal Code s 363 (src:7029-7032)
GIVEN `the person acted with intent to defraud or injure another person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person acted by a false pretence, by s 361(1) the representation is a false pretence` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person causes or induces any person to execute, make, accept, endorse or destroy the whole or any part of a valuable security` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing is a valuable security, by s 2 valuable security` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person causes or induces any person to write, impress or affix a name or seal on any paper or parchment in order that it may afterwards be made or converted into or used or dealt with as a valuable security` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 363 the person commits the offence of obtaining execution of a valuable security by fraud` MEANS
    IF `the person acted with intent to defraud or injure another person`
    THEN `ccc12 and` `the person acted by a false pretence, by s 361(1) the representation is a false pretence`
                     (`ccc12 or` (`ccc12 and` (JUST `the person causes or induces any person to execute, make, accept, endorse or destroy the whole or any part of a valuable security`) `the thing is a valuable security, by s 2 valuable security`)
                                 (JUST `the person causes or induces any person to write, impress or affix a name or seal on any paper or parchment in order that it may afterwards be made or converted into or used or dealt with as a valuable security`))
         -- JUST FALSE where no pretence or neither paragraph holds: FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "who, with intent to defraud or injure another person, by a false pretence causes or induces any person"
         -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): where the s 361(1) or s 2 "valuable security" answer was not given and nothing else settles it
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "who, with intent to defraud or injure another person"

@ref Criminal Code s 363 (src:7030-7030)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 363 the punishment for the offence` MEANS
    LIST `ccc12 an indictable limb` (`imprisonment for a term of` `five years`)
       , `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`

-- src:7033 | Fraudulently obtaining food, beverage or accommodation
-- src:7034 | 364 (1) Every one who fraudulently obtains food, a beverage or accommodation at any place that is in the business of providing those things is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref Criminal Code s 364(1) (src:7033-7034)
GIVEN `the person fraudulently obtains food, a beverage or accommodation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the place is in the business of providing those things` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 364(1) the person commits the offence of fraudulently obtaining food, beverage or accommodation` MEANS
    IF `the person fraudulently obtains food, a beverage or accommodation` AND `the place is in the business of providing those things`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every one who fraudulently obtains food, a beverage or accommodation at any place that is in the business of providing those things"

@ref Criminal Code s 364(1) (src:7034-7034)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 364(1) the punishment for the offence` MEANS
    LIST `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`   -- "is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction": one limb, the summary one

-- src:7035 | Presumption
-- src:7036 | (2) In proceedings under this section, evidence that the accused obtained food, a beverage or accommodation at a place that is in the business of providing those things and did not pay for it and
-- src:7037 | (a) made a false or fictitious show or pretence of having baggage,
-- src:7038 | (b) had any false or pretended baggage,
-- src:7039 | (c) surreptitiously removed or attempted to remove his baggage or any material part of it,
-- src:7040 | (d) absconded or surreptitiously left the premises,
-- src:7041 | (e) knowingly made a false statement to obtain credit or time for payment, or
-- src:7042 | (f) offered a worthless cheque, draft or security in payment for the food, beverage or accommodation,
-- src:7043 | is, in the absence of any evidence to the contrary, proof of fraud.
@ref Criminal Code s 364(2) (src:7035-7043)
GIVEN `the proceedings are proceedings under section 364` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused obtained food, a beverage or accommodation at a place that is in the business of providing those things` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused did not pay for it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused made a false or fictitious show or pretence of having baggage` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused had any false or pretended baggage` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused surreptitiously removed or attempted to remove their baggage or any material part of it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused absconded or surreptitiously left the premises` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused knowingly made a false statement to obtain credit or time for payment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused offered a worthless cheque, draft or security in payment for the food, beverage or accommodation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is evidence to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 364(2) the evidence is proof of fraud` MEANS
    IF    `the proceedings are proceedings under section 364`
      AND `the accused obtained food, a beverage or accommodation at a place that is in the business of providing those things`
      AND `the accused did not pay for it`
      AND (   `the accused made a false or fictitious show or pretence of having baggage`
           OR `the accused had any false or pretended baggage`
           OR `the accused surreptitiously removed or attempted to remove their baggage or any material part of it`
           OR `the accused absconded or surreptitiously left the premises`
           OR `the accused knowingly made a false statement to obtain credit or time for payment`
           OR `the accused offered a worthless cheque, draft or security in payment for the food, beverage or accommodation`)
    THEN IF `there is evidence to the contrary`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is, in the absence of any evidence to the contrary, proof of fraud"
         ELSE JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks of evidence that the accused obtained food, a beverage or accommodation at such a place and did not pay for it and did one of the acts (a) to (f)

DECLARE `s 364(3) kind of instrument` IS ONE OF
    `s 364(3) a cheque in its ordinary meaning`
    `s 364(3) a bill of exchange drawn on an institution that makes it a business practice to honour bills of exchange or any particular kind thereof drawn on it by depositors`
    `s 364(3) another instrument`

-- src:7044 | Definition of cheque
-- src:7045 | (3) In this section, cheque includes, in addition to its ordinary meaning, a bill of exchange drawn on any institution that makes it a business practice to honour bills of exchange or any particular kind thereof drawn on it by depositors.
@ref Criminal Code s 364(3) (src:7044-7045)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 364(3) kind of instrument`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 364(3) the instrument is a cheque` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 364(3) a cheque in its ordinary meaning` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 364(3) a bill of exchange drawn on an institution that makes it a business practice to honour bills of exchange or any particular kind thereof drawn on it by depositors` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 364(3) another instrument` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "cheque includes, in addition to its ordinary meaning, a bill of exchange drawn on any institution ..." does not close the list

-- src:7046 | 365 [Repealed, 2018, c. 29, s. 41]
@ref Criminal Code s 365 (src:7046)
`s 365 as the text shows it` MEANS "365 [Repealed, 2018, c. 29, s. 41]"
